 { White's queenside space advantage severely hinders Black's piece and pawn mobility. Find a powerful three-move piece maneuver to target the base of Black's pawn chain. } 1. { -KEY- } Nd2 $1 { Beginning the journey to a5. } O-O 2. Nb3 $1 Bd8 { Black can, and typically does, challenge White's plan in this fashion. However, now the move Bf4-d6 becomes a tempting option. At the same time, White can still jump a knight to a5 and in so doing undouble their pawn structure. } 3. Na5 $1 { Correct! White lands their knight on a5, and now Black will be forced to part ways with the bishop pair and improve White's pawn structure to prevent the b7 pawn from falling. } Bxa5 4. bxa5 $16 { White stands much better, with the improved structure coupling with the space advantage and bishop pair. } 
