 { Find the best sequence from here. } 1. { -KEY- } c5 $1 Qxb3 2. axb3 $1 { Correct! It's important that White capture with the pawn, since now the semi open a-file will combine with the doubled b-pawns nicely: } a6 3. h3 { White first avoids the bishop from being hunted by ...Nh5. } Nbd7 4. b4 { The threat is b4-b5, exploiting the pin along the a-file. } Rc8 { Black stops the threat, but invites a second typical maneuver which we saw in the previous puzzle. } 5. Nb3 $16 { Black is in serious trouble as they have no good way of defending the b7 pawn. } 
