 { White has more queenside space, but in fact they are overextended. Find the best move for Black. } 1... { -KEY- } Bg4 $1 { Correct! Targeting the knight is very effective, since now the d4 pawn cannot be saved in good circumstances. } 2. Bb5 { White can try to hang on to d4 by pinning the knight, but it comes at the cost of a ruined structure. } ( 2. Nxd5 $2 Qxd2 3. Nxd2 Bxe2 4. Kxe2 Nxd4 { Black is winning here, as White's king is too unsafe and their pieces too uncoordinated to survive an open battle. } ) 
Bxf3 3. gxf3 O-O 4. Bxc6 bxc6 $17 { Black's healthier structure and stronger minor piece leaves them with a clear advantage. In the future, they will aim for the central ...e5 break. } 
