 { Lacking in space, Black has to be very careful to avoid getting steamrolled. Find the only move that holds the balance. } 1... { -KEY- } f5 $11 { Correct! Black shuts things down, knowing that capturing en passant would hurt the integrity of White's structure. As a result, they are able to secure enough space of their own on the kingside to maintain equality. White cannot afford to play gxf6 here since after ...Qxf6 the f4-f5 advance is prevented, and over time the weak light squares on f5 and g4 will allow Black to grab the upper hand. } ( 1... Qf8 { Ignoring it would lead to } 2. f5 $1 { when suddenly Black's pieces lack good squares and White is already winning. } ) 

 1-0

