 ( { Should White play } 0... f5 0. e4 { straight away, or prefer a more patient build-up with } 1. f3 { instead? } ) 
1. { -KEY- } f3 $1 { Correct! White should be patient with their buildup, since in any case Black does not have any serious threats available to them. In general, patience pays off when managing a space advantage. } ( 1. e4 $2 { This move superficially grabs space, but the exchange of central pawns turns out to be favorable for Black: } Nxe4 2. Bxe4 Bxe4 3. Ncxe4 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Nf6 $1 { In general, the space advantage is much more beneficial with more pieces on the board so the multitude of exchanges has helped Black's cause. Additionally, the d5 square is now an outpost while White might also have problems along the vulnerable semi open d-file. } ) 

