 { Black has to be careful about White's extra space on the queenside. Which typical move should they play? } 1... { -KEY- } b6 $1 { Correct! Black immediately undermines the space advantage before White has time to consolidate it. } ( 1... Be7 $2 { In the game this move was played, when after } 2. a3 { now the move } b6 $2 { no longer works, since White can support their pawn chain by playing } 3. b4 $16 { . After 2.a3, } a5 { is best, but that does have the drawback of leaving the b5 and b6 squares very weak. } ) 
2. cxb6 Qxb6 $11 { The position is approximately equal, as Black has active counterplay against White's queenside and central pawns. } 
